# group_bind_reject.tkr — the §9.D capability (c) group-bind REJECT host. Two illegal forms live one per
# namespace under src/, and the single failing build reports every diagnostic it finds, one per scenario
# below. A group-bind `(B | C) as v` covers ONLY the nested member, so a subject `A | (B | C)` whose only
# arm is the group leaves `A` uncovered (rejected); and the parentheses + `as` are the group-bind
# discriminator, so a BARE alternation `B | C as v` still cannot bind (rejected). It has no successful
# build to sanitize/run.

Feature: §9.D group-bind reject — the compiler rejects an uncovered direct member and a binding bare alternation

  Scenario: nonexhaustive — a group-bind match leaving the direct `A` member uncovered is rejected
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "non-exhaustive `match` (cover all cases or add `_`)"

  Scenario: barealt — a bare alternation `B | C as v` that tries to bind is rejected
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "an alternative (`|`) cannot bind; use a separate arm"
